# Build output
bin/
obj/
*.user
.vs/

# Non-redistributable test corpus: real/third-party protected binaries and their runtime DLLs.
# See README "Test corpus" section for why these are never committed.
sample1/
sample2/

# Generated validation/audit output — regeneratable, and historically has contained decompiled
# source of the real protected samples above. Never commit anything from these directories.
.validation-current/
.audit-current/
reports/

# Sample-specific probe tooling (hardcodes real sample1 UI field names) and the internal
# regression suite (hardcodes real sample1/sample2 paths) — not part of the public release.
tools/M5Probe/
AgileDevirtualizer.Tests/

# Orchestration scripts that hardcode the real sample1/sample2 file names/paths (or, for the
# sample2 password check, the crackme's actual password and win-string). The generic scripts
# (validate-common.ps1, build/validate-fault-fixture.ps1, validate-source-fixtures.ps1,
# validate-method-quality-report.ps1, audit-sample1-ilspy.ps1) take assembly paths as parameters
# and stay in the repo; only these hardcode the non-redistributable names.
scripts/validate.ps1
scripts/validate-cast-cleanup.ps1
scripts/audit-sample1-method-quality.ps1
scripts/validate-sample2-password.ps1

# Editor/agent tooling directories, not part of the project itself.
.agents/
.codex/
.claude/
